# The operator's own asset directories at the repository root: the rig files a developer is testing
# with and the .bbmodel sources. Anchored with a leading and trailing slash on purpose — written bare,
# `models` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, which is every single source file in this
# project (pandastic/studio/models/**). The effect was that a new source file was silently invisible
# to `git add`, with `git status` showing nothing and `git check-ignore` the only way to find out.
/rigs/
/models/
